  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Endless Sands",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "passive",
        "description": "<p>Countdown (8). To cross the desert, the party must complete the countdown. It ticks down whenever a PC succeeds on an action roll to navigate the seemingly endless expanse.</p><section id=\"secret-mn0yB3t2n3Agrpn8\" class=\"secret\"><p>How do the PCs travel through the desert? What beyond the extreme distance and lack of water makes this area difficult to cross?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {},
        "originItemType": null,
        "multiclassOrigin": false
      },
      "_id": "1Cg2NBQwZfDHDtud",
      "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/cave-entrance-rocky.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!qSfnKodJHZWYsYKF.1Cg2NBQwZfDHDtud"
    },
    {
      "name": "Water Supply",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "passive",
        "description": "<p>When the party starts their journey, place a number of tokens on this stat block equal to 1 + the number of PCs in the scene. Remove a token at the end of each long rest or when a PC fails an action roll to navigate the desert. When a token would be removed but there are none left, each PC must mark a HP and a Stress. A PC can add a token to this stat block by using a downtime move and making a successful Knowledge Roll to hunt for water.</p><section id=\"secret-HrjAsR0xJqcSmwOJ\" class=\"secret\"><p>What sorts of water-preserving flora or terrain features have the PCs heard might be found in this desert? How do the PCs collect and carry the water they find?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {},
        "originItemType": null,
        "multiclassOrigin": false
      },
      "_id": "1S8CU4cFoFynMX0N",
      "img": "icons/consumables/drinks/wine-amphora-cup-gray.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!qSfnKodJHZWYsYKF.1S8CU4cFoFynMX0N"
    },
    {
      "name": "Shifting Sands",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "passive",
        "description": "<p>The ever-shifting dunes and the whipping wind make trailing creatures through this environment difficult. Action rolls to track creatures through the desert are made with disadvantage.</p><section id=\"secret-quoNT6CadU1q7WDQ\" class=\"secret\"><p>How do the dunes and landscape shift whenever the heroes rest? What is covered or uncovered by the wind?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {},
        "originItemType": null,
        "multiclassOrigin": false
      },
      "_id": "XGtU0hcWUO1rJqSV",
      "img": "icons/skills/trades/academics-merchant-scribe.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!qSfnKodJHZWYsYKF.XGtU0hcWUO1rJqSV"
    },
    {
      "name": "Thunderstorm",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "action",
        "description": "<p><strong>Spend a Fear</strong> to have a torrential downpour soak the land. Each PC must either seek shelter from the storm or collect rainwater. Each PC who seeks shelter marks a Stress. The PCs who collect rainwater make a group action roll.</p><ul><li><p>On a success with Hope, add <strong>1d4</strong> tokens to the Water Supply.</p></li><li><p>On a success with Fear, add 1 token to the Water Supply.</p></li><li><p>On a failure with Hope, each PC who took part in the group action roll marks a Stress.</p></li><li><p>On a failure with Fear, each PC who took part in the group action roll marks a Stress, and the PC who rolled the lowest takes <strong>2d8+4</strong> physical damage from the storm.</p></li></ul><section id=\"secret-zav64YaMGRmiq3pt\" class=\"secret\"><p>How does the storm look to the heroes as it rolls in from miles away? Is the storm natural or unnatural? How can you tell?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {},
        "originItemType": null,
        "multiclassOrigin": false
      },
      "_id": "UNqxbFMJLvgK8bSY",
      "img": "icons/magic/lightning/bolt-forked-teal.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!qSfnKodJHZWYsYKF.UNqxbFMJLvgK8bSY"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sandstorm",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "action",
        "description": "<p><strong>Spend a Fear</strong> to summon a sandstorm that disorients and harries travelers. Each PC takes <strong>2d6+3</strong> physical damage. Until the sandstorm dissipates, a PC who makes an action roll must succeed on an Agility Reaction Roll to avoid the swirl of rocks and debris or take <strong>2d6+3</strong> physical damage.</p><section id=\"secret-J9Dw21CreXbQgtx4\" class=\"secret\"><p>What do the dwellers of this desert wear to weather the sandstorms? How are the dwelling places the party finds here designed to withstand the winds?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {},
        "originItemType": null,
        "multiclassOrigin": false
      },
